[PART 4: OBJECTIVE SCIENTIFIC ASSESSMENT OF GAN AUGMENTATION]
1. Accuracy Trade-Off Finding:
   On canonical Seed 42, accuracy is 94.56% Without-GAN vs 94.54% With-GAN (-0.02%).
   Across multiple seeds, mean accuracy is 91.74% Without-GAN vs 90.05% With-GAN (-1.69%).
   Conclusion: WGAN-GP data augmentation does NOT improve overall MINN accuracy.
2. Genuine Clinical Contribution:
   WGAN-GP balances the minority control class in the genetic training data.
   This consistently improves Sensitivity (Recall) across seeds:
     Seed 42:  95.40% -> 96.52% (+1.12%, reducing false negatives from 115 to 87).
     Seed 101: 97.72% -> 98.36% (+0.64%, reducing false negatives from 57 to 41).
     Mean Sensitivity: 96.56% -> 97.44% (+0.88%).
3. Clinical Context:
   In pediatric neurodevelopmental screening, false negatives carry high developmental costs.
   A slight trade-off in specificity for higher clinical sensitivity is a standard screening paradigm.
